==English==

===Etymology===
From {{confix|en|aero|logy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɛəˈɹɑ.lə.d͡ʒi/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-aerology.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɛɚˈɑ.lə.d͡ʒi/|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒlədʒi|s=4}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ae|ro|lo|gy}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# The branch of [[meteorology]] involving the [[observation]] of the [[atmosphere]] by means of [[balloon]]s, [[kite]]s, [[rocket]]s, [[drone]]s, [[airplane]]s, etc.
# The [[study]] of the [[air]] and of the [[atmosphere]] and technological methods involved. Used in the US Navy until early 1957 to encompass operations as well as scientific knowledge.

